bin/
lib/
obj/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.csv
# ...except the hand-digitised published curves under data/. They are source, not
# output: they cannot be regenerated without re-reading the figures by eye, the test
# suite loads them, and the blanket rule above meant a clone had neither the files nor
# any sign they were missing until eight tests errored.
!data/*.csv

# Input data and run products (large binaries, regenerable)
input/
output/
# Superseded scripts and their outputs, kept locally for reference only
old/
*.npy
environment.yml

# Coverage output. `coverage run` leaves a binary database in the working directory;
# it was committed once by a `git add -A` and is pure noise in a diff.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Packaging artefacts
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
